WEBVTT

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:14.550
"November 15th 11:15 AM"
Comrade Leps, N44's launch has been
scheduled for December 12th.

00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:18.720
"Training Center - Director's Office"
Comrade Leps, N44's launch has been
scheduled for December 12th.

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:24.140
Training continues till the week prior
to launch. That is, three more weeks.

00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:26.520
How is N44's progress?

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:30.690
Excellent. She'll be good
to go by that date.

00:00:30.690 --> 00:00:33.070
I see. Very good.

00:00:33.070 --> 00:00:37.780
Lt. Gen. Viktor, any updates
on the ship or rocket?

00:00:43.790 --> 00:00:44.910
We're short on time! Reduce emergency
rations and other equipment!

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:49.250
"1st Design Bureau"
We're short on time! Reduce emergency
rations and other equipment!

00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:53.260
I want the weight down!
I'll take responsibility, got it?!

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:55.300
--Yes, sir!
--Yes, sir!

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:59.720
To launch N44, who was
much larger than a dog,

00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:03.270
the ship had to be fortified
more than expected.

00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:09.730
Each delayed upgrade increased the chance
the ship wouldn't work as intended.

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:16.280
I can't collapse just yet!

00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:37.340
"Irina: The Vampire Cosmonaut"

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:50.540
"A Promise by the Lake"

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:55.000
"Training Center"

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:56.420
"November 15th 5:15 PM"

00:02:56.420 --> 00:02:56.960
Basically, after orbiting the world
for one hour and 50 minutes,

00:02:56.960 --> 00:02:58.970
"Training Center - Classroom"
Basically, after orbiting the world
for one hour and 50 minutes,

00:02:58.970 --> 00:03:02.180
Basically, after orbiting the world
for one hour and 50 minutes,

00:03:02.180 --> 00:03:06.600
you'll re-enter the atmosphere
and land in Palma Plains.

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:13.230
Like I mentioned, you'll eject from
the ship and descend with a parachute.

00:03:13.230 --> 00:03:19.110
You haven't parachuted on your own,
but you've got three weeks to master it.

00:03:19.110 --> 00:03:25.120
Got it. Can we start training already?
In the centrifuge, right?

00:03:28.580 --> 00:03:30.710
"November 18th 6:05 PM"
That day, the space suit was
delivered to the Training Center.

00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:33.210
"Training Center - Conference Room"
That day, the space suit was
delivered to the Training Center.

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:41.680
Not even the candidates have worn it yet!

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:44.260
Guess I'm the first!

00:03:44.260 --> 00:03:48.140
The equipment was made
for secrecy and durability.

00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:53.100
The bright orange is to locate you,
even if you land in snow.

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:56.690
So hot... and heavy!

00:03:56.690 --> 00:04:01.360
You've gotta wear that when
you parachute, too. Get used to it!

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:12.910
Hey, you're gonna catch a cold.

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:19.920
Huh?! Don't stare!

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:21.760
I-I wasn't!

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:25.470
If you're in charge of me,
where's my change of clothes?!

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:34.020
"Training Center - In Front of Restrooms"

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:43.650
I hear the vampire wore the space suit?

00:04:43.650 --> 00:04:46.490
Yeah, but she looked ridiculous.

00:04:46.490 --> 00:04:50.950
Aren't you annoyed that a vampire
will beat us to the punch?

00:04:50.950 --> 00:04:54.870
And you're helping it happen.

00:04:54.870 --> 00:04:57.290
I'm just doing my duty.

00:04:57.290 --> 00:04:59.750
Duty, huh?

00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:05.760
Whatever. Once her role's over,
the vampire will be disposed of.

00:05:05.760 --> 00:05:09.350
How heart-wrenching
to be aiding her death.

00:05:09.350 --> 00:05:11.430
Don't go saying that.

00:05:11.430 --> 00:05:16.520
She seems awfully obedient.
Maybe she's actually a UK spy?

00:05:16.520 --> 00:05:18.360
She's not that kinda person.

00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:22.320
Person? You think the experiment
is an actual person?

00:05:22.320 --> 00:05:25.400
She's an object. Get it right.

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:32.290
Irina...

00:05:39.250 --> 00:05:43.960
If you have something
to say to me, say it to my face.

00:05:43.960 --> 00:05:47.630
Even if your launch is successful,
I won't acknowledge you.

00:05:47.630 --> 00:05:50.260
I don't care what humans think.

00:05:50.260 --> 00:05:53.430
I don't wanna hear it from a vampire!

00:05:53.430 --> 00:05:55.850
Could you two calm down?

00:05:55.850 --> 00:06:02.440
Hmph! Let's hope you don't die.
Watch out or she'll suck your blood, Lev.

00:06:08.530 --> 00:06:11.620
You overheard us talking?

00:06:11.620 --> 00:06:13.330
Part of it.

00:06:13.330 --> 00:06:18.500
Don't worry about it. Roza is arrogant
and is like that with everyone.

00:06:23.460 --> 00:06:25.590
"Dormitory - Cafeteria"

00:06:29.590 --> 00:06:33.140
Hey, what do you think of me?

00:06:34.430 --> 00:06:38.270
Uh, don't misunderstand.
Not in a weird way.

00:06:38.270 --> 00:06:45.690
People think I'm a spy, but you hardly
ask about me. I'm just curious.

00:06:45.690 --> 00:06:53.160
Well, I don't think you're a spy, but you
do seem obedient for being forced here.

00:06:53.160 --> 00:06:54.330
Forced?

00:06:54.330 --> 00:06:56.700
Huh? Weren't you?

00:06:56.700 --> 00:07:02.960
Not quite. When the UZSR people
came to my village, I volunteered.

00:07:02.960 --> 00:07:04.380
Volunteered?

00:07:04.380 --> 00:07:09.920
Yeah. There were other candidates,
but I came of my own free will.

00:07:09.920 --> 00:07:13.930
You did? I had it wrong then.

00:07:13.930 --> 00:07:17.220
I figured you were abducted
and your family held hostag--

00:07:17.220 --> 00:07:19.180
Don't invent your own story.

00:07:19.180 --> 00:07:23.940
Uh, right. Sorry. But why did you--?

00:07:23.940 --> 00:07:26.820
You're forgetting
to treat me like an object.

00:07:33.280 --> 00:07:35.990
"A Vampire's Day Off

00:07:36.530 --> 00:07:39.540
"November 23rd 9:06 AM
Space Research City 'LAIKA44'"
The Arctic Air Mass known as Moroz
let out an icy breath.

00:07:39.540 --> 00:07:42.670
The Arctic Air Mass known as Moroz
let out an icy breath.

00:07:42.670 --> 00:07:47.050
LAIKA44's long and harsh winter had begun.

00:07:47.050 --> 00:07:49.460
"Belka Lake"
LAIKA44's long and harsh winter had begun.

00:07:51.840 --> 00:07:54.800
"Irina's Confinement Cell"
Next week is solitude training
in the anechoic altitude chamber.

00:07:54.800 --> 00:07:56.720
Next week is solitude training
in the anechoic altitude chamber.

00:07:56.720 --> 00:07:59.640
What was that weird thing you said?

00:07:59.640 --> 00:08:01.850
Anechoic altitude chamber.

00:08:01.850 --> 00:08:08.150
It's a room with increased oxygen
levels and lowered air pressure.

00:08:08.150 --> 00:08:15.160
You can't hear anything, inside or out.
It absorbs sound like the air is dead.

00:08:15.160 --> 00:08:20.160
And you're stuck in there for days
with sensors attached to you.

00:08:20.160 --> 00:08:22.370
What's the point of it?

00:08:22.370 --> 00:08:27.630
Because the cabin you fly in
is cut off from everything.

00:08:27.630 --> 00:08:30.090
It's training for the solitude.

00:08:30.090 --> 00:08:32.340
Another reason is that,
if there're any issues,

00:08:32.340 --> 00:08:37.890
you could be in space for up to a week.

00:08:37.890 --> 00:08:41.060
How long will I be shut in there?

00:08:41.060 --> 00:08:45.940
More than a day, but less than ten.
It's over when the door opens.

00:08:47.810 --> 00:08:54.570
I dread it more than anything else,
so I like to relax or have fun before it.

00:09:01.490 --> 00:09:05.420
Uh, but it's up to you...

00:09:05.420 --> 00:09:08.670
I'm curious; where would you go?

00:09:08.670 --> 00:09:12.510
Me? I sometimes go to the jazz bar.

00:09:12.510 --> 00:09:15.050
The bar? To drink?

00:09:15.050 --> 00:09:17.680
Do you not like alcohol?

00:09:17.680 --> 00:09:21.140
In my village,
we don't drink till we're 20.

00:09:21.140 --> 00:09:22.060
Huh?

00:09:22.060 --> 00:09:24.560
And I'm 17, so...

00:09:24.560 --> 00:09:26.480
Huh? Seventeen? Doesn't your ID say 21?

00:09:26.480 --> 00:09:29.810
"Air Force Private Second Class
Irina Luminesk"
Huh? Seventeen? Doesn't your ID say 21?

00:09:29.810 --> 00:09:34.320
I heard it makes things
easier if I'm an adult.

00:09:34.320 --> 00:09:41.410
No wonder you looked young.
Mmm, good on you for following the rules.

00:09:41.410 --> 00:09:44.160
Anyway, I'm fine with that.

00:09:44.160 --> 00:09:45.120
Huh?

00:09:45.120 --> 00:09:47.750
I'm fine with the jazz bar.

00:09:47.750 --> 00:09:51.290
Do you like jazz?
'Cuz if you don't drink...

00:09:51.290 --> 00:09:54.590
That's not--! Um, I...

00:09:56.010 --> 00:10:03.220
You don't know what it is? Still, there're
other drinks, too, and music as well.

00:10:03.220 --> 00:10:04.560
But why--?

00:10:04.560 --> 00:10:07.230
Whatever! Just take me there!

00:10:17.030 --> 00:10:20.030
"November 25th 7:05 PM"

00:10:24.410 --> 00:10:27.000
First time seeing you in plain clothes.

00:10:27.000 --> 00:10:29.040
Makes me antsy.

00:10:29.040 --> 00:10:30.040
Me, too.

00:10:30.040 --> 00:10:32.250
Me, too.

00:10:32.250 --> 00:10:33.550
It's cold.

00:10:33.550 --> 00:10:34.800
Not really.

00:10:42.760 --> 00:10:45.270
"Jazz Bar 'Zvezda'"

00:10:54.270 --> 00:10:56.400
Hmm? What's that?

00:10:56.400 --> 00:11:01.360
Huh? Oh, that's a phonograph.

00:11:01.360 --> 00:11:04.740
It plays music with the spinning disc.

00:11:04.740 --> 00:11:07.290
I've never heard this music.

00:11:07.290 --> 00:11:11.920
Jazz being from the United Kingdom,
it was banned to play,

00:11:11.920 --> 00:11:14.880
but it was made legal not long ago.

00:11:24.930 --> 00:11:27.640
What's the name of this song?

00:11:27.640 --> 00:11:29.140
"My Beloved."

00:11:29.140 --> 00:11:33.520
I like it. Not that I know
what they're saying.

00:11:36.570 --> 00:11:38.990
Should we order some drinks?

00:11:41.400 --> 00:11:44.370
To think you'd order soda water...

00:11:44.370 --> 00:11:46.700
I'll drink it just for you.

00:11:46.700 --> 00:11:49.080
She likes it after all.

00:11:49.080 --> 00:11:50.580
What?

00:11:50.580 --> 00:11:52.330
Oh, nothing.

00:11:57.500 --> 00:11:59.800
I hate to admit, but it's good.

00:12:13.690 --> 00:12:15.480
What? I said it's good.

00:12:15.480 --> 00:12:17.070
No, it's...

00:12:21.650 --> 00:12:25.870
What kind of drink is that?
It's a pretty red.

00:12:25.870 --> 00:12:33.120
Nastoyka--of oleaster soaked for
three weeks in <i>zhizni</i>. Want a sip?

00:12:33.120 --> 00:12:36.500
Nope. I told you, I'm 17.

00:12:36.500 --> 00:12:44.090
Here in the UZSR, drinking age is 16.
You might like it as much as soda water.

00:12:44.090 --> 00:12:47.550
Hmm. Just a sip then.

00:12:52.060 --> 00:12:55.190
M-My mouth! My tongue is burning!

00:12:56.770 --> 00:12:59.650
I'm not ready for that yet.

00:13:09.990 --> 00:13:11.490
Hey, Lev.

00:13:11.490 --> 00:13:15.620
Huh? Lev? She called me by my name...

00:13:15.620 --> 00:13:18.460
Did you hear me? Wh-Whoa!

00:13:21.840 --> 00:13:24.510
Sorry! You okay?

00:13:24.510 --> 00:13:26.050
I'm fine.

00:13:31.010 --> 00:13:36.190
Hey, Lev. When did you first
wanna go to space?

00:13:36.190 --> 00:13:37.400
Huh?

00:13:37.400 --> 00:13:38.940
I wanna know.

00:13:41.480 --> 00:13:42.980
When I was five.

00:13:42.980 --> 00:13:44.400
Five?

00:13:44.400 --> 00:13:49.240
Yeah. I saw an airplane crossing
in front of the full moon.

00:13:49.240 --> 00:13:52.160
I thought a plane could take me there.

00:13:52.160 --> 00:13:56.670
It seems dumb looking back,
but that's what I thought.

00:13:56.670 --> 00:14:02.960
I just wanna go to the Moon.
UK cosmonauts probably think the same.

00:14:02.960 --> 00:14:09.760
And yet, for how beautiful space is,
the world is ugly and dirty.

00:14:09.760 --> 00:14:13.180
We shouldn't bring war into space!

00:14:15.770 --> 00:14:17.390
They'll arrest you.

00:14:17.390 --> 00:14:20.020
Natalia! What are you doing here?

00:14:20.020 --> 00:14:24.860
Hmm? You expect me to live
in the kitchen making soup?

00:14:24.860 --> 00:14:28.490
No, I just wasn't expecting to see you.

00:14:30.530 --> 00:14:35.250
More importantly, you should
keep it down about the UK.

00:14:35.250 --> 00:14:38.750
The Delivery Crew might be listening.

00:14:38.750 --> 00:14:40.040
Sorry.

00:14:41.080 --> 00:14:45.760
Poor Irina here has to deal
with "Snow Thaw" Lev.

00:14:45.760 --> 00:14:47.260
Snow Thaw?

00:14:47.260 --> 00:14:49.880
Natalia! Don't mention that!

00:14:49.880 --> 00:14:56.020
He gets so heated up when talking
about space, people say he thaws snow.

00:14:56.020 --> 00:14:57.680
Oh?

00:14:57.680 --> 00:14:59.270
What?

00:15:00.350 --> 00:15:03.860
Sorry for interrupting
your day off together.

00:15:03.860 --> 00:15:06.900
--It's not...
--...like that!

00:15:06.900 --> 00:15:09.150
See you later, you two.

00:15:17.200 --> 00:15:18.830
Well, what next?

00:15:18.830 --> 00:15:20.620
What else is there?

00:15:20.620 --> 00:15:25.340
A movie, billiards...
And skating, I guess.

00:15:34.760 --> 00:15:38.930
Welcome, Comrade Leps.
What brings you here?

00:15:38.930 --> 00:15:41.100
To look at your ice skates.

00:15:41.100 --> 00:15:43.060
--What?!
--What?!

00:15:44.770 --> 00:15:48.490
I guess Roza's not
the only pretty soldier...

00:15:48.490 --> 00:15:51.860
You have such unique and pretty eyes!

00:15:54.280 --> 00:15:57.910
Private Luminesk! Pick out
the training gear and let's go!

00:15:59.620 --> 00:16:02.080
Huh? Private?

00:16:14.510 --> 00:16:17.470
"Belka Lake"

00:16:19.640 --> 00:16:21.390
It's all ours!

00:16:21.390 --> 00:16:24.560
Nobody's skating on a night this cold.

00:16:25.610 --> 00:16:27.020
Won't you?

00:16:27.020 --> 00:16:29.070
I'm here to monitor you.

00:16:30.490 --> 00:16:31.900
Hey, hold on!

00:18:16.880 --> 00:18:18.720
That was fun!

00:18:23.970 --> 00:18:31.690
Going to space seems so far-fetched.
Though, being a reserve, I can't anyway.

00:18:31.690 --> 00:18:33.860
Why are you a reserve?

00:18:36.280 --> 00:18:39.110
I thought you had high marks.

00:18:40.780 --> 00:18:43.490
I was violent toward a superior.

00:18:43.490 --> 00:18:45.040
Violent?

00:18:45.040 --> 00:18:47.250
The son of an engineer chief
blamed a new graduate

00:18:47.250 --> 00:18:52.880
for their own failure and got him fired.

00:18:52.880 --> 00:18:58.760
The graduate was apologizing, and yet,
that only got his head stepped on.

00:18:58.760 --> 00:19:01.930
I couldn't hold back and charged in.

00:19:01.930 --> 00:19:04.060
That's "Snow Thaw" Lev for you.

00:19:04.060 --> 00:19:06.430
Could you not call me that?

00:19:08.890 --> 00:19:11.900
Hmm? What's up?

00:19:11.900 --> 00:19:15.940
Experiment subjects are disposed of, huh?

00:19:17.860 --> 00:19:19.700
You heard that?

00:19:22.410 --> 00:19:26.410
To humans, I wonder what we are?

00:19:29.830 --> 00:19:37.800
When I was three, my parents got caught up
in the war and were burned to death.

00:19:37.800 --> 00:19:40.630
A lot of the villagers were killed.

00:19:42.640 --> 00:19:47.640
The meaning of my name... is "peace."

00:19:47.640 --> 00:19:50.390
And yet, why?

00:19:52.350 --> 00:19:56.320
Did you know vampires are
"People of the Moon"?

00:19:56.320 --> 00:20:00.240
Yeah. I believed it when I was little.

00:20:00.240 --> 00:20:05.950
Since we're People of the Moon,
we're hated on this planet.

00:20:05.950 --> 00:20:11.370
<i>Lunny kamen. </i>This moonstone
was passed down for generations.

00:20:11.370 --> 00:20:15.840
Sinus Iridum, Lacus Somniorum,
Palus Somni...

00:20:15.840 --> 00:20:22.430
Oceanus Procellarum, Mare Vaporum,
Palus Putredinis, Sinus Fluctus...

00:20:26.220 --> 00:20:33.230
I wanted to take this stone to the Moon,
but I don't have wings and can't fly.

00:20:33.230 --> 00:20:37.320
But then, the UZSR people showed up.

00:20:37.320 --> 00:20:42.400
I'm fine with being an experiment
or using the power of humans.

00:20:42.400 --> 00:20:44.070
I just wanted to go to space.

00:20:46.780 --> 00:20:52.830
So that's why she's put up with
training without a single complaint.

00:20:52.830 --> 00:20:56.250
Ever since then, you...

00:21:01.340 --> 00:21:03.840
I wanna go to space before a human!

00:21:03.840 --> 00:21:04.930
Huh?

00:21:04.930 --> 00:21:09.680
If I can do that,
I don't care if I'm disposed of.

00:21:09.680 --> 00:21:14.690
I just want to see the Moon
before humans defile it.

00:21:14.690 --> 00:21:19.150
So, stick with me a little while longer.

00:21:19.150 --> 00:21:23.400
Of course. I'll take you to space.

00:21:23.400 --> 00:21:26.660
No matter what happens, I'm your ally.

00:21:28.530 --> 00:21:34.580
You're a weird person...
But I'm glad it's you monitoring me.

00:21:35.620 --> 00:21:38.170
I think I'll skate more!

00:21:38.170 --> 00:21:39.380
Okay.

00:21:40.000 --> 00:21:43.010
"November 26th 6:07 PM"

00:21:43.510 --> 00:21:47.430
"Training Center - Hallway"
I can't remember anything about yesterday.

00:21:47.430 --> 00:21:50.680
You got back from the lake and slept.

00:21:50.680 --> 00:21:52.640
What lake?

00:21:52.640 --> 00:21:54.390
Oh, Irinyan...

00:21:58.270 --> 00:22:00.020
Being isolated from humans? I welcome it.

00:22:00.020 --> 00:22:02.030
"Training Center -
Anechoic Altitude Chamber"
Being isolated from humans? I welcome it.

00:23:48.800 --> 00:23:51.010
"Next episode:
'Training Separately'"
